  "minutes": 8,
  "gear": "1 puck per pair",
  "worksAsStation": true,
  "description": "The coach shows the press (pinning the puck flat with your blade) and the lift (lifting the other stick off the puck). Partners stand side by side. On the first whistle one player handles the puck in place; on the second the partner tries to press the puck or lift the stick. This is stick checking only: no body contact, and sticks stay below the knees.",
  "steps": [
    "First whistle: O handles the puck, standing still.",
    "Second whistle: X presses the puck flat or lifts O’s stick.",
    "Switch jobs and go again."
  ],
  "cues": [
    "Stick checks only, no bodies.",
    "Lift from under the other stick.",
    "Win the puck, then switch."
  ],
